## Tests

All three go in `crates/tools/src/spec.rs`, `mod tests`. Copy them exactly, because the fixture line numbers matter. Use only these ids in fixtures: every `R<n>` in this file must have a note (rule 3), and R3, R4, R5, R14 and R58 all do.

```rust
    #[test]
    fn refuses_a_ruling_marker_whose_sentence_links_no_ruling() {
        let path = "spec/02-core-systems.md";
        let text = [
            "**Ruling:** the Nth empty draw deals N damage. It is reported ([[R3]]).",
            "| Hand | Cap 10 (ruling) | [[R4]] |",
            "5. Player 1 draws on turn 1 (**Ruling**, Hearthstone convention).",
            "**Ruling (rotation topology):** a ring.",
            "**Ruling:** attacks are not lane-restricted ([[R5]]). Lanes matter for adjacency.",
            "| Hand | Cap 10 (ruling, [[R4]]) |",
            "**Ruling ([[R58]]):** one draw casts at most one.",
            "**Ruling (rotation topology, [[R14]]):** a ring.",
            "A ruling or a section written before the rename, and the rulings of §11.",
            "`(ruling)` is code, and a link before a marker ([[R3]]) is not its link (ruling).",
            "```text",
            "**Ruling:** inside a fence.",
            "```",
        ]
        .join("\n");
        let found = unlinked_markers(path, &text);
        let lines: Vec<&str> = found.iter().map(|f| f.split(':').nth(1).unwrap_or("")).collect();
        assert_eq!(lines, vec!["1", "2", "3", "4", "10"]);
        assert!(found[0].starts_with(&format!(
            "{path}:1: a ruling marker whose sentence links no ruling"
        )));
    }

    #[test]
    fn holds_only_the_notes_of_sections_two_to_ten_to_their_markers() {
        for path in ["spec/02-core-systems.md", "spec/08-catalog.md", "spec/10-engine-guide.md"] {
            assert!(is_marked_section(path), "{path}");
        }
        for path in [
            "spec/01-overview.md",
            "spec/11-rulings.md",
            "spec/13-duos.md",
            "spec/README.md",
            "spec/INDEX.md",
            "spec/rulings/R0003.md",
        ] {
            assert!(!is_marked_section(path), "{path}");
        }
    }

    #[test]
    fn check_fails_on_an_unlinked_ruling_marker_until_it_links_its_ruling() {
        let root = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("jackioh-spec-markers-{}", std::process::id()));
        let _ = fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        fs::create_dir_all(root.join("spec").join("rulings")).unwrap();
        fs::create_dir_all(root.join("crates")).unwrap();
        fs::write(root.join("crates").join("fatigue.rs"), "#[test]\nfn r3_fatigue() {}\n").unwrap();
        fs::write(
            root.join("spec").join("rulings").join("R0003.md"),
            "---\nid: R3\ntitle: Fatigue effect\ncards: \"§2.4\"\nproven_in:\n  - crates/fatigue.rs\n---\nNth empty draw deals N damage to your hero\n",
        )
        .unwrap();
        index(&root).unwrap();
        let section = root.join("spec").join("02-core-systems.md");
        fs::write(&section, "## 2. Core systems\n\n**Ruling:** the Nth empty draw deals N damage.\n").unwrap();
        let unlinked = check(&root);
        fs::write(&section, "## 2. Core systems\n\n**Ruling:** the Nth empty draw deals N damage ([[R3]]).\n").unwrap();
        let linked = check(&root);
        let _ = fs::remove_dir_all(&root);
        assert_eq!(unlinked.unwrap_err().to_string(), "spec check: 1 problem(s)");
        assert!(linked.is_ok(), "{linked:?}");
    }
```

What each test checks:
- **`refuses_a_ruling_marker_whose_sentence_links_no_ruling`.** These must be flagged: a link that comes only in the next sentence (line 1), only in the next table cell (line 2), or only before the marker (line 10), and a marker with no link at all (lines 3 and 4). These must pass: links inside every marker form (lines 5–8), plain prose and `rulings` (line 9), markers in code spans, and fenced code.
- **`holds_only_the_notes_of_sections_two_to_ten_to_their_markers`.** Only §2–§10 are read.
- **`check_fails_on_an_unlinked_ruling_marker_until_it_links_its_ruling`.** The command itself fails with exactly one problem, and passes once the link is added. This is acceptance item 1.

Commands:

```
cargo test -p jackioh-tools --bin jackioh spec::tests
cargo test -p jackioh-tools
cargo clippy -p jackioh-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt --check
cargo jackioh spec check
cargo jackioh spec index && git status --porcelain -- spec/INDEX.md
cargo jackioh classify --base origin/main --claims
```

- `spec check` must print `… links: ok`.
- `spec index` must leave `spec/INDEX.md` unchanged, so `git status` prints nothing.
- `classify` should find no card that plays differently and no fragment, so it passes.

## Done when

- [ ] `spec check` fails on an unlinked marker. `check_fails_on_an_unlinked_ruling_marker_until_it_links_its_ruling` passes, and the other two new tests pass.
- [ ] All 20 markers in step 7 carry their ruling's link, and `cargo jackioh spec check` prints `ok` on the tree.
- [ ] No ruling note was added, and `spec/INDEX.md` is unchanged after `spec index`.
- [ ] `cargo test -p jackioh-tools`, the clippy and `fmt --check` runs above, `catalog check` and `patches check` are all green. Each red check is reported by name.
- [ ] The PR body records the decisions below, including R4 over R317 and sentence scope over line scope.

## Risks

- **A false positive on a future marker.** The sentence ends at the first `. ` (period then space). A marker sentence holding "e.g. " before its link would be flagged. The fix is to put the link before the abbreviation; never loosen the rule. No marker in §2–§10 has this today: the planner ran this exact code on the tree and found exactly the 20 sites, and none after the edits.
- **Other readers of the edited text.** `apps/web/src/cards/rules.test.ts` reads only the first column of `spec/06-keywords.md`. `crates/cards/tests/cross/catalog.rs` reads only the token tables of `spec/07-tokens.md`, and lines 159–160 are bullets after them. Nothing parses `spec/08-catalog.md`. Edit only the third and later cells, and never add a `|`.
- **Rule 3 on `spec.rs` itself.** Every `R<n>` written in the new code and tests needs an existing note. Use only R3, R4, R5, R14 and R58.
- **The test's temp directory.** It is named per process, and the test removes it before asserting, so a failed assertion leaves nothing behind.
- There are no engine, determinism, replay or hidden-information effects: the change touches only the tools crate and the spec's prose.

## Open questions

None block the build. These decisions were made for the PR body:

1. **The link must be in the marker's own sentence**, from the marker to the first `. `, ` |` or the line's end. The rejected alternative was the whole line or cell. Under it, 02:9 (R9), 02:55 (R3), 02:56 (R4), 04:11 (R7) and 06:115 (R15) pass on an unrelated ruling's link elsewhere on the line. The cost is that 03:22, which the issue cites as the convention, gains `([[R5]])` in its first sentence.
2. **The hand cap (02:56, 03:7) links R4**, the "Hand size (decide)" ruling, not R317 as the issue suggested. R317 is about who sees a burned card. It stays linked where it is.
3. **Marker forms.** `ruling` as a whole word counts as a marker after `(`, before `:`, or before ` (…):`, in any case, with `*` read through. The rejected alternative was matching only the literal `(ruling)` and `Ruling:`, which misses `(**Ruling**, Hearthstone convention)` (02:11) and `**Ruling (rotation topology):**` (03:24).
4. **No new ruling and no reworded marker.** Every marker has a note, from the original §11 table's R3–R50.
5. **REVIEW.md A2.3 is left as written.** Its other half, the §8 indices and the "decide" rows, is still checked by hand.
